1
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:21,000
Heroes are ordinary men who do extraordinary things in extraordinary times.

2
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:36,000
U-571 is a war, action, adventure film directed by Jonathan Mostow.

3
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:51,000
In the midst of World War II, the battle under the sea rages and the Nazis have
the upper hand as the Allies are unable to crack their war codes.

4
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:06,000
However, after a wrecked U-boat sends out an SOS signal, the Allies realise
this is their chance to seize the 'enigma coding machine'.

5
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:21,000
Lt. Andrew Tyler, played by Matthew McConaughey.

6
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:36,000
Lt. Cmdr. Mike Dahlgren, played by Bill Paxton.

7
00:50:45,000 --> 00:50:51,000
CPO Henry Klough, played by Harvey Keitel.

8
00:58:00,000 --> 00:58:06,000
Lt. Pete Emmett, played by Jon Bon Jovi.

9
01:05:15,000 --> 01:05:21,000
Maj. Matthew Coonen, played by David Keith.

10
01:12:30,000 --> 01:12:36,000
Capt. Lt. Gunther Wassner, played by Thomas Kretschmann.

11
01:19:45,000 --> 01:19:51,000
U-571 is a 2000 submarine film directed by Jonathan Mostow from a
screenplay he co-wrote with Sam Montgomery and David Ayer.

12
01:27:00,000 --> 01:27:06,000
The film stars Matthew McConaughey, Bill Paxton, Harvey Keitel,
Jon Bon Jovi, Jake Weber and Matthew Settle.

13
01:34:15,000 --> 01:34:21,000
The film follows a World War II German U-boat boarded by American
submariners to capture her Enigma cipher machine.

14
01:41:30,000 --> 01:41:36,000
Although the film was financially successful and received generally positive reviews from critics, winning the Academy
Award for Best Sound Editing, the fictitious plot was subject to substantial controversy and criticism.

15
01:48:45,000 --> 01:48:51,000
The film explores themes of mission, submarine, world
war ii, north atlantic, enigma machine.
